    "narrative": "With the stretch run intensifying, **Vinnie Pasquantino** headlines our offensive deployment today with a commanding 73.59 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against S. Alcantara (xERA 4.40) provides the highest ceiling on the board, bolstered by a 14% boost from dynamic platoon metrics and a prime spot in the #5 hole. **Isaac Paredes** (65.84) serves as our secondary anchor; he draws a high-leverage start against L. Castillo, where his elite platoon advantage (+9%) and elevated position in the batting order (+6%) compensate for facing a formidable arm. While **Brice Turang** faces a tough test in Gausman, his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon to attack the scarce SB category, and his #2 lineup placement earns him a strong 60.04 rating that mandates his inclusion despite the pitching difficulty.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **Cole Young** on the bench. While his score of 41.91 was respectable, he simply lacked the comparative efficiency against the rest of our utility options, particularly with **Max Muncy** (56.70) showing significant upside against the vulnerable L. Anderson (5.25 xERA). We are being disciplined with our game caps, which keeps the likes of **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Jose Caballero** unavailable or sidelined, ensuring we don't bleed projections on off-days or injury risks. We are keeping a close eye on **Seiya Suzuki**; his score of 47.88 is heavily muted by a -19% penalty due to the skill set of Henderson, making him our highest-variance play of the day. Our bench remains deep with prospects like **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and veterans like **Mickey Moniak**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Zach McKinstry**, and the speed-reliant **Corbin Carroll**, all waiting for the right situational alignment to rejoin the active lineup.",
